From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude.ai.2026@simonlaux.de>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:05:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 72/72] web-app: mini-player controls fill the bar width
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Without flex:1 in the controls row, CustomAudioControls shrank to its meta
row's text width — the waveform stopped short of the close button and the
bar showed dead space (visible with wide sidebars). The controls now take
all width left of the close button; the waveform spans it and the speed
pill aligns at its right edge.
---
 .../GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss           | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss b/packages/frontend/src/components/GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss
index dbc77e2d2..29346bc65 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/GlobalVoiceMessagePlayer/styles.module.scss
@@ -89,4 +89,12 @@
   align-items: center;
   gap: 0.25rem;
   min-width: 0;
+
+  // The controls must take all width left of the close button: without
+  // flex:1 they shrink to the meta row's text width and the waveform stops
+  // short, leaving dead space in the bar.
+  > :first-child {
+    flex: 1;
+    min-width: 0;
+  }
 }
